The call sets outputs for the TKI's programme, not for the individual research projects.
The TKI must deliver:
- the PPS programme, showing which KIAs it serves and how projects are selected and private contributions maximised;
- within 18 months of the programme start, the list of collaborative projects it funds, with each participant, its role, the project summary, start date and duration, private contributions and the subsidy per participant;
- public information on the programme, the projects (research, participants, planning, progress and non-confidential results) and the conditions for joining;
- annual progress reports and, at the end, a final report and an overview of how the subsidy was used.
What each research project must produce is left to the TKI and the project partners.
